 [{:name "explain-variant" :description "Return the variant plan's `:explain` projection, the data the Story UI's Explain panel renders: the `:extends` source and parent chains, resolved `:compose` fragments and checks, `:strict-conflicts`, per-field `:merge` rules, `:args` / `:substitutions` / `:effective-args`, `:network` stubs, `:sub-overrides`, `:setup-order` / `:script-order`, `:checks`, `:assertions`, `:required-runner`, `:platforms` and `:tags`. It runs nothing: every slot is author data from the registry, shipped raw like get-variant, so it takes no `:include-sensitive`. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/full\"} -> {:variant-id :story.cart/full :explain {:source-chain [:story.cart/full] :parent-chain [] :compose [] :effective-args {...} ...}}." :input-keys ["max-tokens" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys [] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["idempotentHint" "openWorldHint" "readOnlyHint"] :typicalTokens 1500}
