  {:name "preview-variant" :description "Run a variant headlessly and return its canvas state and a shareable URL: {:variant-id :share-url :status :lifecycle :app-db :assertions :checks :effective-args :snapshot ...}. `:status` (:pass :fail :cannot-run :error) is the verdict; `:lifecycle` (:ready / :error) is the loader state. It runs the same lifecycle as run-variant and refuses the same way (isError): no installed re-frame adapter gives `:rf.error/no-adapter-installed`; an unknown `:active-modes` id or `:cell-overrides` key is named with the accepted set, never dropped. `:timeout-ms` defaults to 10000 and clamps to 30000; an overrun returns `:status :error`. Values are projected through the frame's classification: a sensitive path reads `:rf/redacted`, an oversize slot `:rf.size/large-elided`. Rendered output is not included. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/full\" :active-modes [\":mode/dark\"]} -> {:variant-id :story.cart/full :share-url \"...\" :status :pass :lifecycle :ready :app-db {...} :assertions [] ...}." :input-keys ["active-modes" "base-url" "cell-overrides" "dedup" "include-sensitive" "max-tokens" "substrate" "timeout-ms" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys ["include-sensitive"] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["destructiveHint" "openWorldHint"] :typicalTokens 2000}
  {:name "read-a11y-violations" :description "Re-read the axe-core results a variant's in-browser a11y panel last stored. It runs no check, so it proves nothing about a variant the panel has not inspected. Returns {:variant-id :violations [...] :incomplete [...]}: `:incomplete` holds the checks axe could not decide, so `:violations []` beside a non-empty `:incomplete` is not a clean bill. Each node carries `:html`, `:target` and `:failureSummary`; a value at a classified app-db path redacts, but one rendered into node `:html` ships as rendered. Listed only on a host that reaches the panel state. Example: {:variant-id \":story.form/checkout\"} -> {:variant-id :story.form/checkout :violations [{:id \"label\" :impact \"critical\" :nodes [...]}] :incomplete []}." :input-keys ["include-sensitive" "max-tokens" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys ["include-sensitive"] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["idempotentHint" "openWorldHint" "readOnlyHint"] :typicalTokens 500}
  {:name "read-failures" :description "Re-read, without re-running, the assertion records a variant frame accumulated in its latest run: {:variant-id :status :total :failures :assertions}, in run-variant's record shape, with `:failures` holding the `:fail` / `:error` records. `:status` aggregates the records alone (no epoch tape, so no agreement floor: re-run run-variant for the full verdict), including any record dropped as sensitive, which `:dropped-sensitive` counts. A registered variant that never ran reads {:status :pass :total 0}. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/bad\"} -> {:variant-id :story.cart/bad :status :fail :total 5 :failures [{:assertion :rf.assert/sub-equals :passed? false :status :fail :reason \"...\"}] :assertions [...]}." :input-keys ["include-sensitive" "max-tokens" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys ["include-sensitive"] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["idempotentHint" "openWorldHint" "readOnlyHint"] :typicalTokens 500}
  {:name "register-variant" :description "Register a variant, the write step of the write, run, read-failures, fix loop. Gated: refused with isError and structuredContent {:gated true :tool \"register-variant\"} unless the server was started with `--allow-writes` (or `-Drf.story-mcp.allow-writes=true`, or `RF_STORY_MCP_ALLOW_WRITES=true`). `:body` is a JSON object, or an EDN string when the body needs keywords or sets. Registering an existing id replaces it. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/probe\" :body \"{:doc \\\"probe\\\" :tags #{:dev}}\"} -> {:variant-id :story.cart/probe :registered? true}." :input-keys ["body" "max-tokens" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys [] :required ["body" "variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["destructiveHint" "openWorldHint"] :typicalTokens 100}
  {:name "run-variant" :description "Run a variant's lifecycle (loaders, setup, render, script) headlessly and return the unified run-result the Story UI reads. `:status` (:pass :fail :cannot-run :error) is the verdict; `:cannot-run` means the plan could not be attempted here, not that it failed. The result also carries `:assertions` (each with its own `:status`), `:checks`, the evidence slots (`:schema-violations :warnings :effects :sub-runs :renders :narrative`), `:app-db`, `:snapshot`, `:elapsed-ms`, and `:plan-hash` / `:run-hash`, equal across reruns of a deterministic scenario. Refusals (isError): no installed re-frame adapter gives `:rf.error/no-adapter-installed` (install one in the namespace your launch alias preloads, e.g. `(rf/init! plain-atom/adapter)`); an unknown `:active-modes` id or `:cell-overrides` key is named with the accepted set, never dropped. `:timeout-ms` defaults to 10000 and clamps to 30000; an overrun returns `:status :error`. Values are projected through the frame's classification: a sensitive path reads `:rf/redacted`, an oversize slot `:rf.size/large-elided`, and effect and event args redact. A `:narrative` beat carries a `:trace-event-count`; `:include-trace-events true` ships the raw events (raise `max-tokens`). Rendered output is not included. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/bad\"} -> {:status :fail :frame :story.cart/bad :assertions [{:assertion :rf.assert/sub-equals :passed? false :status :fail :actual nil :expected 3}] :checks [] :elapsed-ms 42 ...}." :input-keys ["active-modes" "cell-overrides" "dedup" "include-sensitive" "include-trace-events" "max-tokens" "substrate" "timeout-ms" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys ["include-sensitive"] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["destructiveHint" "openWorldHint"] :typicalTokens 2000}
  {:name "snapshot-identity" :description "Return the content hash of a variant's identity tuple (variant, resolved args, decorators, loaders, modes, cell-overrides, substrate): {:variant-id :active-modes :substrate :content-hash}. It is stable across hosts, so it keys visual regression, and `:cell-overrides` change it through the resolved args. An unknown `:active-modes` id or `:cell-overrides` key is refused (isError naming it and the accepted set), never dropped from the tuple. Runs nothing. Example: {:variant-id \":story.cart/full\" :active-modes [\":mode/dark\"]} -> {:variant-id :story.cart/full :active-modes [:mode/dark] :substrate nil :content-hash \"sha256:abcd...\"}." :input-keys ["active-modes" "cell-overrides" "max-tokens" "substrate" "variant-id"] :gated-input-keys [] :required ["variant-id"] :output? true :annotations ["idempotentHint" "openWorldHint" "readOnlyHint"] :typicalTokens 100}
